{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_cYOLbUZu0xwaRs2XdMdMwgJQ","content":"1\t# Literature host interfaces · plan r6, amended at close\n2\t\n3\t**Status: r6 draft, 2026-11-23. Not approved; r6's own bytes are not\n4\treviewed.** The owner selected the full GND review panel (D14, ruled `(o)`),\n5\tand it ran twice. The first round read r4 (sha256\n6\t`6cadaa9134585b348d53ef50ef5c35638a3b0bb20c7c36726ac53039ac357cb6`): four of\n7\tsix reviewers succeeded, all asking for revision, with twelve ranked fixes\n8\t([r4 record](../../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/README.md)).\n9\tr5 applied them, tagged `(p1)`. The second round read r5 (sha256\n10\t`c1a832378a2f303cdf1be8884ea61e745eca7f22e4fab19a449761d62b082c9b`): five of\n11\tsix succeeded, one approving and four asking for revision, with seven ranked\n12\tfixes ([r5 record](../../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r5-panel/README.md)).\n13\tr6 applies those, tagged `(p2)`. §11 maps every fix of both rounds to its\n14\tsites. The convergence rules allow no third panel round. The owner's rulings on D6, D9 and D10 (2026-11-22, r3) and on D14 and\n15\tD17 (2026-11-23, r4 and r5) are tagged `(o)`. r2 to r4 were never committed.\n16\tNo plan-gate record exists. The owner gates the plan before any spec is\n17\tapproved and before any code.\n18\t\n19\tThis plan covers [#216](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/216)\n20\tand [#215](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/215). It delivers\n21\tthe interface half of the \"host-scale reading and extraction\" carryover from\n22\tthe [literature-depth close](../../literature-depth/016-milestone-close.md).\n23\tThe run over a separately selected corpus and provider budget stays carried\n24\twith the literature-identity follow-up, as that close assigned it.\n25\t\n26\t**Provenance.** Outline r1 is the previous bytes of this file (sha256\n27\t`abefb05f7fa7c19d068182eeeb557efea36bbc89d555647d98ec350b1017bea0`, commit\n28\t`0cf94434`, merged in PR 219). Its phase IDs LH1–LH4 and decisions D1–D3 are\n29\tkept. Its reviews, `.gnd-planning/reviews/pr-219-r2/` and `pr-219-panel/`,\n30\tread the roadmap outline, not these bytes. The r4 panel's opinion covers r4's\n31\tbytes only, and the r5 panel's covers r5's; no sentence new in r6 carries a\n32\treview opinion. Every code citation was re-read on 2026-11-22 at `4ad0d216`,\n33\tand those r5 and r6 add or correct on 2026-11-23 at the same commit;\n34\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/` is unchanged since `0f39c392`, where the outline\n35\tcited it. The outline wrote the two module paths without `src/gnd/`; they are\n36\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py` and\n37\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/assertion_admission.py`. Below, `reading.py`,\n38\t`assertion_admission.py` and `depth.py` mean the files in that folder.\n39\t\n40\t## Goal and completion predicates\n41\t\n42\tA host with its own corpus and its own model calls the two literature examples\n43\tas library functions instead of reimplementing them. The examples stay\n44\texamples: neither is promoted to stable CLI (both issues say so).\n45\t\n46\t- **LH1.** `reading.py` has a public producer protocol. `run()` drives the six\n47\t  stages with a caller's producer over a caller's input root: its own\n48\t  documents, its own reading model with its own includes, no saved responses\n49\t  and no producer pin. Each of the fixture-only steps runs on caller data or\n50\t  is recorded as skipped. The run has a byte budget per document as well as\n51\t  the global one, and its caps are parameters. The responses and review\n52\t  receipts a live run produces are retained in its run folder.\n53\t- **LH2.** `replay()` re-derives a live LH1 run from its run folder and the\n54\t  caller's input root with zero producer calls and zero reviewer calls. It\n55\t  takes every setting from the run, and refuses a changed response, receipt or\n56\t  input.\n57\t- **LH3.** `assertion_admission.py` admits assertions of a caller-named entity\n58\t  in a caller's model. An assertion is identified by its own handle `(o)`.\n59\t  Every fact row attached to an admitted assertion is kept, whatever its fact\n60\t  type, together with the facts of the entities reached from it `(o)`. Absent\n61\t  optional facts are simply absent. An include root is admitted.\n62\t- **LH4.** Which values make a supported assertion admissible is caller data.\n63\t  A supported assertion that fails those rules has a status of its own. The\n64\t  target cap is a parameter.\n65\t\n66\tThe milestone is closed when each phase has its record and the close record\n67\tcites green focused lanes for LH1–LH4, the structure and inventory guards,\n68\tthe whole-repository `uv run ruff check`, as `project.md` requires `(p1)`,\n69\tthe replies drafted for #216 and #215, and the close review. Baseline, measured 2026-11-22 at `4ad0d216`\n70\twith gnd 0.4.0:\n71\t`uv run pytest -q tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py\n72\ttests/test_ld5_verdict.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py\n73\t--tb=short` gave `90 passed in 166.21s`; `uv run ruff check src tests tools`\n74\texits 0. The whole-repository `uv run ruff check` exited 1 at `4ad0d216`,\n75\twith all 198 findings in the scripts delivered from dev-tools (H25). The owner\n76\thad them fixed upstream: dev-tools PR 34, merged as `a29562a`. After\n77\t`devtools/sync.py apply` from that commit, the whole-repository lint exits 0\n78\tand the gate-guard and scaffold tests pass (measured 2026-11-23). The re-sync\n79\tis committed with this plan, so LH1 starts from a `main` where the whole\n80\trepository lints clean `(p1)`: the start condition in §3 is that commit, not\n81\t`4ad0d216` `(p2)`.\n82\t\n83\t## 0. Binding design rules\n84\t\n85\t- **R0.1 Formats stay.** The stage record (`stage-N.json`), the attempt rows\n86\t  and their three outcomes, and the coverage rows with their eight states are\n87\t  unchanged; #216 says they work as they are. `literature-rebind/1` belongs to\n88\t  `interop.py` and is not touched.\n89\t- **R0.2 Packaged bytes stay.** With no new argument, the three packaged\n90\t  reading run configurations (`full`, `--scenario unavailable` and\n91\t  `--budget-bytes 0`; `SCENARIOS` itself has two values, `reading.py:38`)\n92\t  `(p1)` and the packaged admission write the bytes they write today. The comparison goes through `tests/support/recorded_version.py`,\n93\t  because the reading run retains two fidelity reports that carry\n94\t  `gnd_version` (H11).\n95\t- **R0.3 Example status stays.** Public here means named in the example's\n96\t  README and covered by tests. No `gnd` subcommand is added, and the two\n97\t  module command lines keep every argument they have.\n98\t- **R0.4 One loop, one walk.** Reading: the caller route and the packaged\n99\t  route run the same stage loop; the packaged constants become default data\n100\t  for it, not a second copy of it (standing rule 4). Admission `(p1)`: the\n101\t  D10 ruling keeps the packaged model, whose `assertion` objectifies a fact\n102\t  type, out of the generic projection, so admission has two projections, the\n103\t  packaged one as it is today and the generic attached-and-followed one. They\n104\t  share everything else, each in one home: the snapshot and the\n105\t  `gnd judgments check` route (`_judgments`, `_verify_report_inputs`), the\n106\t  mapping from a target's verdicts to a support reason (the target half of\n107\t  `_support`), the admission-rule evaluator of LH4, and the record writer and\n108\t  publication. The packaged projection gains no feature of the generic one;\n109\t  it stops at the packaged shape, as it does today.\n110\t- **R0.5 A setting is retained evidence.** Every argument that shapes a caller\n111\t  run is written into the run. Replay reads settings from the run, never from\n112\t  its caller.\n113\t- **R0.6 Skipped is not passed.** A step the caller did not supply is recorded\n114\t  with the status `skipped`. No report presents it as qualified, as measured\n115\t  or as zero.\n116\t- **R0.7 The stable commands stay the judges.** `gnd extract`, `verify`,\n117\t  `check`, `fidelity` and `judgments check` are invoked as today. Neither\n118\t  example re-implements one of their checks or widens one of their caps.\n119\t- **R0.8 A parameter has a ceiling.** Each cap that becomes a parameter has a\n120\t  hard maximum fixed in its spec, and a time-bound test at that maximum\n121\t  (standing rule 2).\n122\t\n123\tThe project's six standing rules\n124\t(`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`) bind every phase; each\n125\tspec discharges them by name.\n126\t\n127\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n128\t\n129\tHarvested obligations. \"Observed\" means re-read or run on 2026-11-22 at\n130\t`4ad0d216`; \"inherited\" means claimed by a source and not re-measured;\n131\t\"proposed\" means new in this plan.\n132\t\n133\t| # | Source | Obligation | Kind | Phase |\n134\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n135\t| H1 | #216 \"Problem\" | `run()` (`reading.py:562`) builds `SavedProducer(inputs.responses)` at `:566`; only the private `_evaluate(..., producer=)` at `:445` takes another | observed | LH1 |\n136\t| H2 | `reading.py`, `ReadingInputs` | the root is bound to saved responses by the pin (`:72-75`, \"saved producer table differs from its pin\") and by the roster check (`:113`, \"saved response roster differs\"), and to the packaged vocabulary (`:135`) | observed | LH1 |\n137\t| H3 | `reading.py`, stage loop | the fixture bindings: the outline's six, the producer label and, found by the panel, the calibration path's literals `(p1)`: the `unavailable` scenario names `study-methods` (`:448`); `_calibrate` names that section, the fact `approximation` (`:317`) and `CALIBRATION_FACTS` (`:42`, `:311-327`), and the absence floor is the literal `[2, 2]` (`:372`); and the calibration path also fixes its renderer label `authored-public-fixture` (`:300`), its case folders `run-methods` and `held-back-predicate` (`:320`, `:323`) and its count of two cases (`:335`) `(p1)`; `_combined` adds `LABEL` to every population (`:48`, `:247`); `_public_results` needs `conflict.json`, `conflict.txt`, a `subject_label` fact with exactly two labels and exits 1 from `verify` and `check` (`:395-407`); `absence_status` needs the predicate `alternative_integrator` (`:373`); `_review_attempts` needs a `reviews.json` receipt bound to each accepted response's facts digest (`:198-209`); the extraction sidecar names its producer `saved-public-fixture` (`:264`) | observed | LH1 |\n138\t| H4 | `reading.py`, producer boundary | `produce(stage, section)` gets two names and no source bytes (`:156`); the loop reads a `calls` attribute from the producer (`:457`). `_inspect` accepts exactly three outcomes, `accepted`, `empty`, `refused` (`:185`). The outline's \"and the existing others\" was wrong: the other five coverage states are decided by the loop before or without a call | observed | LH1 |\n139\t| H5 | `depth.py:21-30`, `:56`, `:61` | three fixture-scale limits the outline did not list: every input file, source documents included, is read with a 128 KiB cap (`INPUT_LIMIT`); every JSON input is capped at 1 MiB; every `gnd` route has 30 seconds and 1 MiB of output (`PROCESS_LIMITS`). A caller document over 128 KiB refuses at read. Replay reads the run's own files through the same `_read` (`reading.py:414-437`), and each `payload-N.json` embeds every response of its stage (`:190-192`), so two 64 KiB responses already make a payload replay cannot read `(p1)` | observed | LH1 (D4) |\n140\t| H6 | `reading.py:27-30`, `:86`, `:263`, `:298`, `:384-387` | file names are fixed: the eleven `INPUTS` are all required; a source's path must be `<id>.txt`; the model must be `reading.orm.json` with one include named `vocabulary.orm.json`; the artifact names `reading.orm.projection.schema.json` and `reading.orm.applicable.json` are literals. Probe: `gnd extract caller.orm.json` on a renamed copy exits 0 and names its artifacts `caller.orm.*` | observed | LH1 |\n141\t| H7 | `reading.py:386`; include-root-routes IR2 | the loop runs `gnd extract` on the reading model after the producer has answered. `gnd extract` refuses a temporal model. A caller's reading model must be one `gnd extract` accepts, and a refusal there should cost no producer call | observed | LH1 |\n142\t| H8 | `reading.py:473-478`, `:172-174` | the global \"stop\" is a reason computed after the loop; the only thing that ends reading early is the byte budget, which omits sections. \"Per document\" has no present meaning | observed | LH1 (D6) |\n143\t| H9 | #216 \"Request\" | producer protocol, live and replayable; stop rule per document; roster cap and byte budget as parameters; `replay()` against a caller root | inherited | LH1, LH2 |\n144\t| H10 | consumers of `reading.py` | `revision.py:171` calls `reading.replay(retained, fixture=inputs, vocabulary_fixture=inputs)` and `:62-64` reads `reading.FIXTURE` and `reading.DEPTH_FIXTURE`; `assurance_report.py:760` calls `replay(run_dir)` with no root and `:725` caps coverage rows at 128 `(p1)`; the tests patch `SavedProducer.produce`, `_read` (on the replay path, `test_ld3_reading_workflow.py:238-246`) and `_public_results`, call `_inspect` directly with six positional arguments and read `producer.calls` (`:153-165`) `(p1)`, and read `ROSTER_LIMIT` | observed | LH1, LH2 |\n145\t| H11 | probe, 2026-11-22 | no test pins the bytes of a packaged reading run. `fidelity-high.json` and `fidelity-low.json` carry `gnd_version`. Evidence digests at gnd 0.4.0: `full` `ee67e13c…fd1c`, `--scenario unavailable` `d4010f94…6ddf`, `--budget-bytes 0` `7dcf43ec…a071` | observed | LH1 |\n146\t| H12 | #215 \"Problem\" | `project()` (`assertion_admission.py:100`) accepts three fact types only (`:105`); every role is a mandatory non-empty string (`:45-52`); absence is a sentinel (`:30`, `:84`); identity is (work, passage) (`:55-63`, `:111-113`); the admissible pair is