| A raised cap turns a legal input into minutes of CPU | R0.8; LH1-C10, LH3-C9 |\n449\t| A live run retains files that its own replay cannot read `(p1)` | a `/2` run bounds its files before the first call and records its cap; LH1-C14, LH2-C3 |\n450\t| The retained-file bound refuses runs that work today `(p2)` | the bound applies to `/2` runs only, and a `/2` run's default cap is derived from its own bounds; LH1-C9, LH1-C14 |\n451\t| The generic admission path drifts from the packaged one `(p1)` | R0.4 names the shared homes; LH4-C6 runs the packaged rules through the one evaluator |\n452\t| A rule quantified \"any\" or \"every\" passes on fixtures that cannot tell them apart | LH3-C3, LH3-C4 and LH4-C3 each hold the discriminating case |\n453\t| A host reads \"parameter\" as \"no limit\" for `MAX_TARGETS` | LH4-C4; the README and the #215 reply state the stable ceiling |\n454\t| A large caller vocabulary exceeds the route timeout ([#221](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/221)) | the timeout is a limit (D4); a route that times out refuses naming the route |\n455\t| LH1 is larger than one phase | its spec states the size; if the estimate passes 400 source lines the spec proposes a split at its gate, with new IDs LH1a and LH1b |\n456\t| The packaged bytes pin moves at a version bump | the comparison uses `tests/support/recorded_version.py`, with `RECORDED_AT = \"0.4.0\"` |\n457\t\n458\t## 7. Out of scope\n459\t\n460\tThe corpus and provider-budget run; stable-CLI promotion of either module; a\n461\tchange to `gnd judgments check`'s caps or to any stable command; batching\n462\tinside `admit()`; the assurance scorer's row cap; admission of an entity that\n463\tobjectifies a fact type under a shape (D10, ruled); following an entity type\n464\tthe shape does not list (D17, ruled); #218, #221, #222;\n465\trelease, tag and publication.\n466\t\n467\t## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol\n468\t\n469\t- The plan review is held to the project's bar, the maintained GND review\n470\t  panel. The owner selected the full panel (D14, ruled `(o)` 2026-11-23); its\n471\t  first round read r4 and, at the owner's request, its second round read r5.\n472\t  The convergence rules allow two rounds at most, so r6 goes to the plan gate\n473\t  without a third `(p2)`.\n474\t- The plan gate is recorded in `001-plan-gate.md` once the owner rules, with\n475\t  the review's instrument, reviewed digest and dispositions, or the statement\n476\t  that none ran.\n477\t- Execution is `process-milestone literature-host-interfaces`, or\n478\t  `process-phase LH1 literature-host-interfaces` for one phase. `auto=true`\n479\t  needs the owner's explicit delegation for this milestone; none has been\n480\t  given (D15).\n481\t- Each phase: spec, spec gate, code, focused gates, one independent reviewer\n482\t  over the diff (D13), refactoring review, record, commit.\n483\t- Two pull requests (close A2): the reading pair (LH1, LH2) from\n484\t  `claude/literature-host-interfaces`, then the admission pair (LH3, LH4)\n485\t  from `claude/literature-host-interfaces-admission`, each to `main`. Before\n486\t  it, `python3 scripts/components_index.py changed --base origin/main\n487\t  --strict` exits 0. Merge stays with the owner.\n488\t\n489\t## 9. Per-phase verification\n490\t\n491\t| Phase | Focused lane | Expected |\n492\t|---|---|---|\n493\t| LH1 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh1_reading_host.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py tests/test_ld5_verdict.py tests/test_li1_assurance_report.py --tb=short` | exit 0 |\n494\t| LH2 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh2_reading_replay.py tests/test_lh1_reading_host.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py tests/test_ld5_verdict.py tests/test_li1_assurance_report.py --tb=short`, then `uv run python tools/run_tutorials.py --group literature` | exit 0 each |\n495\t| LH3 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py --tb=short` | exit 0 |\n496\t| LH4 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh4_admission_rules.py tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py --tb=short`, then `uv run python tools/run_tutorials.py --group literature` | exit 0 each |\n497\t| all | the structure and inventory guard block of `project.md`, and the whole-repository `uv run ruff check` `(p1)` | exit 0 |\n498\t\n499\tAffected consumers named here are read at each spec and may be widened there.\n500\tNo broad lane (`-m \"evidence or census\"`) is selected.\n501\t\n502\t## 10. Owner decisions and open questions\n503\t\n504\tD6, D9 and D10 carry the owner's ruling of 2026-11-22 `(o)`, and D14 and D17\n505\tthe rulings of 2026-11-23 `(o)`. Every other row is a proposal until the plan\n506\tgate rules it. D1–D3 keep their outline IDs; D4–D16 are new in r2, D17 in r3\n507\tand D18 in r5. r6 adds none.\n508\t\n509\t| ID | Question | Proposed | What the other reading costs |\n510\t|---|---|---|---|\n511\t| D1 | Where the producer protocol lives | In `reading.py`, until a second example uses it | A shared module now is a public home with one user |\n512\t| D2 | Name and reach of the LH4 disposition | `policy-refused`, in the `/2` record only; `/1` keeps `fail` | Applying it to `/1` changes the packaged record's bytes and `test_li4`'s expectations |\n513\t| D3 | The fixture-only steps on a caller root | Calibration, the conflict check and the absence scope are optional and declared in the profile; an undeclared step is `skipped`. The population label is profile data. A reviewer is optional, and a decision other than `supported` refuses the run | A reviewer that filters instead needs a ninth coverage state, which changes the row format #216 asks to keep |\n514\t| D4 | Which caps become parameters, and their ceilings | Seven limits `(p1)`: roster cap (default 128, ceiling 4,096), largest budget (1 MiB, 64 MiB), per-file input (128 KiB, 8 MiB), response (128 KiB, today's effective bound, since a response cannot exceed the 128 KiB read of `responses.json`; ceiling 1 MiB), route timeout (30 s, 600 s), route output (1 MiB, 16 MiB), retained file (for `/2` runs only `(p2)`: derived from the run's own bounds and never less than 128 KiB, today's read of a run's own files; ceiling 10 MiB, the repository's JSON read cap `gnd.input_policy.MAX_BYTES` (close A1)). The ceilings cannot all be reached together: at the 1 MiB response ceiling a retained file holds fewer than 10 eligible sections `(p2)` (close A1). A JSON file is decoded under its read cap. `document_budget` is a `run()` argument whose ceiling is the largest-budget limit | #216 names the first two only; with only those, a source over 128 KiB still refuses, a slow `gnd check` still stops the run at 30 s, and a live run can retain files its replay cannot read (H5) |\n515\t| D5 | Manifest format of a caller run | `literature-reading-run/2` for any run that uses a new argument; `/1` unchanged otherwise | Optional keys in `/1` let an older reader accept a run it cannot re-derive |\n516\t| D6 | What \"the stop rule per document\" means | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-22: as proposed.** A byte budget per source, enforced in the loop, and a stop reason per source in the report. A document whose required questions are resolved still gets its other scheduled reads | Ending a document at required coverage reads less, and changes which optional questions are answered; it could be a later switch |\n517\t| D7 | A malformed response, or a producer that raises | Refuse the run with nothing written; a host that prefers to continue returns `refused` from its own producer | Recording it as `refused` reports a transport failure as the producer's verdict |\n518\t| D8 | LH3: what is judged, and how row verdicts make an assertion's verdict | Targets are attached rows; supported means at least one target and every target admitted | \"Any target admitted\" admits an assertion with a rejected participant row |\n519\t| D9 | LH3: how far \"hangs off\" reaches | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-22: the other reading, follow entities outward.** Not adopted: directly attached fact types only; they form `covers`; other fact types are not copied | Following entities outward keeps a quantity entity's own facts, at the price of a reachability rule the model does not state. That rule is D17 |\n520\t| D10 | LH3: linking an objectified fact's row to its handle | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-22: the other reading, own handle only.** Not adopted: a link through the preferred external uniqueness, each identifying role matched to a role of the same name and object type in the objectified fact type | No rule means the objectified form is refused and only entities with their own handle are admitted, which leaves the packaged model on the old path only |\n521\t| D11 | LH4: the ceiling of `max_targets` | 1,024, the stable command's cap; a larger set is admitted in several calls the host makes | Raising `judgments.py`'s caps changes a stable command; that would be its own issue |\n522\t| D12 | LH3: the record of a shaped call | `literature-assertion-admission/2`; the packaged call keeps `/1` | One format with optional keys makes `lineage_run.py:254` accept records it was not written for |\n523\t| D13 | Phase diff reviewer | The review helper (`.claude/skills/process-phase/scripts/review_tool.py`, subject `phase`), one reviewer in a different tool | none; this is `project.md`'s default |\n524\t| D14 | Plan-review instrument | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-23: the full GND panel** (\"full\"). Its first round read r4, its second r5 | none |\n525\t| D15 | How the milestone runs | The owner selects: phase by phase with an owner gate on each spec, or `process-milestone … auto`. Ruled at the plan gate as phase by phase; superseded on 2026-11-23 by the owner's `/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto` (close A3) | none |\n526\t| D16 | LH1: which `verify` and `check` exits let a caller run complete | 0, 1, 2 and 4 are