126b35b4b2e60887ac8996e3abfadbaed647\n33\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py\n34\t    sha256: cad2bea4aa679310e154f98bcdad3e85e89cba581812ba703f059d737246d8b6\n35\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/assurance_report.py\n36\t    sha256: eb5bf73f97b9a7f400ae4c68348334fd8dfba932ceea5b585341f74da3d56078\n37\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/reading_fixture/README.md\n38\t    sha256: 797c060777fd392dee286322c38b45ac4faf79df08847f50dbe46acf449c57c7\n39\t  - path: tests/test_lh2_reading_replay.py\n40\t    sha256: 84f9895071d52affdceff71defc02d8ff75f8c7cb6136d27832cd067ed8d7983\n41\t  - path: tests/test_lh1_reading_host.py\n42\t    sha256: c0db56071a7f2f5c17ff521949c748b3aaf7f5b2656950b698741ff1b19cc5fe\n43\t  - path: docs/literature/commands.md\n44\t    sha256: 9d7f3d092c276124d8df27689abbad397d912922f7d34ee8f7b3c72a60470181\n45\t  - path: docs/release-notes.md\n46\t    sha256: 3fde981b1b7c920b17cae776352b7bdda18a358df90b40b37e601e4270a3f62e\n47\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH2-r1/review.md\n48\t    sha256: 066aed2030be6d523d8d0df9a083bde32cda16f12559400cb80ac2ce9530ea3a\n49\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH2-r1/FINDINGS.md\n50\t    sha256: 5736726aaeffba3890039819e20712b559e644fe7d8cbe7d6aab2890f63da674\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t# Phase LH2: replay of a caller run\n54\t\n55\t## Claim\n56\t\n57\t`replay(folder, fixture=root)` re-derives a `literature-reading-run/2`\n58\tfolder from its own files and the caller root, with no producer and no\n59\treviewer, and refuses every changed file, changed input, malformed manifest\n60\tand out-of-ceiling setting. Criteria and their tests in\n61\t`tests/test_lh2_reading_replay.py`:\n62\t\n63\t| Criterion | Tests |\n64\t|---|---|\n65\t| LH2-C1 | T1 (a plain live run and a declared run with a live reviewer, replayed byte-identical with zero calls) |\n66\t| LH2-C2 | T2 (one changed byte in the response table and in a receipt; a consistently rewritten folder with and without the expected digest) |\n67\t| LH2-C3 | T3 (lowered and raised limits with a document budget; the 9-section run at the response ceiling within 60 s; `route_seconds` 601) |\n68\t| LH2-C4 | T4 (source, profile, model and include each refuse \"stale reading input\") |\n69\t| LH2-C5 | `test_ld3`, `test_ld4`, `test_ld5` unedited, in the focused lane |\n70\t| LH2-C6 | T6 |\n71\t| LH2-C7 | T7 |\n72\t| spec §6.1 | T8: a `/2` folder under the packaged root and a `/1` folder under a caller root each refuse by name |\n73\t| rule 1, rule 3 | T9 (seven malformed manifests refuse before any run file; every run file read under the recorded cap; saved and empty live runs replay), R1 to R3 |\n74\t\n75\t## Gate\n76\t\n77\tDelegated approval (auto=true), 2026-11-23, under the owner's\n78\t`/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto`, of the spec at sha256\n79\t`2e15cb11…4ef8` (commit `33fe059b`), LH2-D1 and LH2-D2 as proposed. The\n80\tspec has since been appended only. The milestone coordinator's GO for LH2\n81\tconcerned file order with literature-reading-reference and approved\n82\tnothing.\n83\t\n84\t## Review\n85\t\n86\tOne reviewer is one reviewer: Codex in the other harness, read-only,\n87\tthrough `review_tool.py`, one round over the LH2 diff (base `33fe059b`).\n88\tThree findings, all reproduced, one blocking and two hardening, none\n89\tself-inflicted; all fixed at `9df661c8` with regression tests that failed\n90\tbefore the fix. The convergence rules did not call for a second round, so\n91\tthe repairs carry no review opinion. The retained review was sanitized of\n92\tthis machine's paths, as its header says.\n93\t\n94\t## Refactoring review\n95\t\n96\tRefactors EXECUTED, behavior-preserving behind the unedited `test_ld3`,\n97\t`test_ld4`, `test_ld5`: the stage-chain and file reading of a run moved into\n98\tone helper, `_retained_files`, shared by the `/1` and `/2` readers, and now\n99\tdecodes each file under the cap it was read with. Deferred: none.\n100\t\n101\t## Refuted premises\n102\t\n103\t**Plan D4's 64 MiB retained-file ceiling.** Every JSON reader in the\n104\trepository goes through `gnd.input_policy`, which refuses JSON over 10 MiB\n105\t(`MAX_BYTES`). LH1's run at the response ceiling (63 sections, a 63 MiB\n106\tpayload) completed and could not be read back, contradicting LH1-C14 and\n107\tLH2-C3. Repaired in this phase by delegated approval: the ceiling is\n108\t`gnd.input_policy.MAX_BYTES`, imported, and the ceiling runs use 9 sections\n109\t(spec finding 1). The plan text is repaired at milestone close (open\n110\tquestion Q1).\n111\t\n112\t## Open questions\n113\t\n114\t| ID | Question | Owner | Target |\n115\t|---|---|---|---|\n116\t| Q1 | Plan §10 D4 and §2 LH1 still say the retained-file ceiling is 64 MiB; the shipped ceiling is the JSON read cap, 10 MiB | milestone close | plan repair at close |\n117\t\n118\t## Boundary\n119\t\n120\t- **The reading pair ends here.** LH1 and LH2 are delivered as the first of\n121\t  two pull requests (README, deviation from plan §8).\n122\t- **No review reads `9df661c8`'s repairs.**\n123\t- **A consistently rewritten folder replays** unless the host passes the\n124\t  digest `run()` returned; the README says so.\n125\t- **Out of scope.** No command-line flag for a caller root; `revision.py`'s\n126\t  packaged replay is unchanged."}
