ngs\n106\t\n107\tNone refuted. Spec findings 1 to 5 record the departures from the letter:\n108\tinclude paths read with the model parser, cases built in the test module,\n109\tthe `venue` entity, T9's 60 s bound, and T8's four digests. Review found\n110\tthat handles must be keyed as the checker keys them\n111\t(`gnd.synth.identity.scalar_identity`), not as Python keys.\n112\t\n113\t## Open questions\n114\t\n115\tNone opened by this phase.\n116\t\n117\t## Boundary\n118\t\n119\t- **Rules, `policy-refused` and `max_targets` are LH4's.** A shaped call\n120\t  without rules admits every supported assertion.\n121\t- **Nested includes are not copied.** An include root whose include\n122\t  declares includes refuses through the judgment route.\n123\t- **`instances` is `{}`** in the admitted population (LH3-D3).\n124\t- **No review reads round 2's repair.**\n125\t- **Out of scope.** No command-line flag; no change to `gnd judgments\n126\t  check`."}
