8\t| LH4-C6 | T6 (default rules passed explicitly: same reasons, order and admitted bytes, `policy-refused` for statements 3 to 6); LH3's T8 pins the four H18 digests of the call with no argument |\n69\t| LH4-C7 | T7 (each of shape, rules, `max_targets`, `max_rows` changes its field; a rules-only call records `packaged`, `null`, `null`) |\n70\t| rule 2 | T8 (64 requirements over 65,536 rows within 60 s) |\n71\t\n72\t## Gate\n73\t\n74\tDelegated approval (auto=true), 2026-11-23, under the owner's\n75\t`/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto`, of the spec at sha256\n76\t`ed5f1be1…712c` (commit `8fffc161`), LH4-D1 and LH4-D2 as proposed. The\n77\tspec has since been appended only. The coordinator's GO for LH4 approved\n78\tnothing.\n79\t\n80\t## Review\n81\t\n82\tOne reviewer is one reviewer: Codex in the other harness, read-only,\n83\tthrough `review_tool.py`, one round over the LH4 diff (base `8fffc161`).\n84\tTwo findings, both reproduced, one blocking and one hardening, none\n85\tself-inflicted; both fixed at `4428a24d` with regression tests that failed\n86\tbefore the fix. The convergence rules did not call for a second round; the\n87\trepairs carry no review opinion. The retained review was sanitized of this\n88\tmachine's paths, as its header says.\n89\t\n90\t## Refactoring review\n91\t\n92\tRefactors EXECUTED, behavior-preserving behind LH3's T8, LH4's T6 and the\n93\tunedited `test_li4`, `test_li5`: the literal comparison of\n94\t`project()` (`(polarity, attribution) != (\"asserts\", \"own-finding\")`) became\n95\t`DEFAULT_RULES` evaluated by `_evaluate_rules`, the one evaluator of both\n96\tprojections (R0.4). Deferred: none.\n97\t\n98\t## Refuted premises and findings\n99\t\n100\tNone refuted. Spec findings 1 to 4: `reasons` is a list of value and reason\n101\tpairs, not a mapping keyed by JSON text; the model loads before the judgment\n102\troute, so an edited include refuses `input:model` (LH3's T5 updated); the\n103\t`/2` record names the shape kind; `_case` gained `edit_model`.\n104\t\n105\t## Open questions\n106\t\n107\tNone opened by this phase.\n108\t\n109\t## Boundary\n110\t\n111\t- **Rules name attached fact types only**, never followed ones.\n112\t- **1,024 targets per call** is `gnd judgments check`'s cap; a larger set is\n113\t  admitted in several calls the host makes (D11).\n114\t- **No review reads `4428a24d`'s repairs.**\n115\t- **Out of scope.** No command-line flag; no change to `gnd judgments\n116\t  check`."}
