{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_6qDgewhIy7Uh8wcnJ9gsEb0E","content":"1\t# Literature host interfaces\n2\t\n3\tPlan r6, 2026-11-23, from [issue #216](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/216)\n4\tand [issue #215](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/215).\n5\t**Plan approved by the owner on 2026-11-23** ([plan-gate record](001-plan-gate.md),\n6\tr6 sha256 `2dc760e5…1528`), with every decision ruled. The full panel\n7\treviewed r4 and r5; r6 answers the second round and is not itself reviewed.\n8\tNothing is implemented, and no phase spec is approved.\n9\t\n10\t| Phase | Deliverable | State |\n11\t|---|---|---|\n12\t| LH1 | A public producer protocol in the reading example; a caller's producer drives the six stages over a caller's root, with a budget per document, caps as parameters and optional steps recorded as skipped | done: [record](002-phase-LH1.md), [spec](notes/phase-LH1-spec.md) |\n13\t| LH2 | `replay()` of a live run from its own folder and the caller's root, with zero producer calls and its settings read from the run | done: [record](003-phase-LH2.md), [spec](notes/phase-LH2-spec.md) |\n14\t| LH3 | Admission over a caller-named assertion entity, identified by its own handle: every attached fact row kept, the facts of followed entities kept with them, include roots admitted | done: [record](004-phase-LH3.md), [spec](notes/phase-LH3-spec.md) |\n15\t| LH4 | Admission rules as data, the status `policy-refused`, and `max_targets` as an argument up to 1,024 | done: [record](005-phase-LH4.md), [spec](notes/phase-LH4-spec.md) |\n16\t\n17\t[Plan](notes/literature-host-interfaces-plan.md). Third in the\n18\t[roadmap after 0.4.0](../../PROJECT.md#roadmap-after-040--planned-2026-11-21):\n19\tthe reporter has working workarounds for both issues.\n20\t\n21\tThree things the plan found that the outline did not say:\n22\t\n23\t- The reading loop completes only when `gnd verify` and `gnd check` exit 0.\n24\t  A caller model with a constraint over a fact type not yet read exits 2, so\n25\t  the loop as written cannot finish on such a model (plan H23, decision D16).\n26\t- `gnd judgments check` itself stops at 1,024 targets per policy. A\n27\t  `MAX_TARGETS` parameter cannot admit more than that in one call (plan H13,\n28\t  decision D11).\n29\t- The checker does not join an objectified fact type to its entity (plan\n30\t  H14). The owner ruled that admission identifies an assertion by its own\n31\t  handle and refuses an entity that objectifies a fact type (D10).\n32\t\n33\tOwner rulings so far: D6 as proposed (a budget and a stop reason per\n34\tdocument; no early end at required coverage); D9, follow entities outward\n35\tfrom an admitted assertion; D10, own handle only; D17, as proposed (the host\n36\tlists the entity types to follow, and nothing else is followed).\n37\t\n38\tPlan review: the owner selected the full GND panel (D14) on 2026-11-23. It\n39\tran over plan r4 (sha256 `6cadaa91…7cb6`): four of six reviewers succeeded,\n40\tall asking for revision, with two blocking concerns and twelve ranked fixes\n41\t([panel record](../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/README.md)).\n42\tPlan r5 applies all twelve (plan §11). For the lint conflict the owner had\n43\tthe dev-tools scripts fixed upstream (dev-tools PR 34, merged as `a29562a`),\n44\tand gnd-public is re-synced, so the whole-repository lint exits 0 again. The\n45\tLH1 spec is brought to r5. r5's own bytes are not reviewed; r5 is not\n46\tapproved. Plan r5 adds one proposed decision, D18 (the admission row bound).\n47\t\n48\tSecond round: the owner asked for it on 2026-11-23. It ran over r5\n49\t(sha256 `c1a83237…2c9b`), and five of six reviewers succeeded:\n50\t\n51\t- Gemini approved.\n52\t- Claude, Codex, Kimi and GLM asked for revision.\n53\t- Qwen timed out.\n54\t\n55\tThree concerns reached agreement:\n56\t\n57\t- LH1-C14's run at the response and roster ceilings cannot fit the retained-file ceiling.\n58\t- §3 starts LH1 at `4ad0d216`, before the lint re-sync.\n59\t- LH1-C10 misses two of the seven ceilings.\n60\t\n61\tOne blocking concern came from a single reviewer (Claude): under D4's\n62\tdefaults, the retained-file bound refuses the packaged runs. Seven fixes are\n63\tranked in the\n64\t[round-two record](../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r5-panel/README.md),\n65\tand plan r6 applies all seven (plan §11, tagged `(p2)`). The main change:\n66\tthe retained-file bound applies only to new-format (`/2`) runs, whose default\n67\tcap is derived from their own bounds, so today's runs keep their path and\n68\tbytes. The LH1 spec is brought to r6. r6 adds no decision. This was the last\n69\tpanel round the convergence rules allow.\n70\t\n71\tPlan gate, 2026-11-23: the owner ruled the other thirteen decisions as\n72\tproposed (\"All as proposed\"), with D15 phase by phase (`auto=false`).\n73\t\n74\tNext action, the owner's: commit the planning work (the plan's §3 start\n75\tcommit is the merge that lands it with the dev-tools re-sync); then review and\n76\tgate the LH1 spec, which also rules LH1-D1 to LH1-D5; then select\n77\t`process-phase LH1 literature-host-interfaces`.\n78\t\n79\tExecution: the owner delegated the milestone on 2026-11-23\n80\t(`/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto`), which supersedes D15's\n81\tphase-by-phase ruling. Branch `claude/literature-host-interfaces`.\n82\t\n83\t**Deviation from plan §8, two pull requests.** Plan §8 delivers the milestone\n84\tas one pull request. It is delivered as two: the reading pair (LH1 and LH2),\n85\tthen the admission pair (LH3 and LH4), so that literature-reading-reference's\n86\tLR3, which needs LH1 and LH2 on `main`, need not wait for LH4. The\n87\tmilestone-coordinator session (local_0bf324b1) relayed the owner's answer to\n88\t\"Accept splitting literature-host-interfaces into two PRs?\" as \"Accept the\n89\tsplit\". This session did not receive those words from the owner directly; it\n90\trecords the split as a delegated amendment (auto=true) under the owner's\n91\tmilestone delegation, with the relayed words as their source. Merging each\n92\tpull request stays with the owner."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_MYLkdoUzIxBdOozVOA0lWdb6","content":"1\t# Drafted replies to #216 and #215\n2\t\n3\tDrafted at milestone close for the owner to post (plan §5). Not posted.\n4\t\n5\t## #216: drive the reading example from a host\n6\t\n7\tThe reading example now takes your producer. Put a `profile.json` in a\n8\troot beside your roster, your `<id>.txt` sources and your reading model with\n9\tits includes, and call:\n10\t\n11\t```python\n12\tfrom gnd.examples.literature import reading\n13\treport = reading.run(out, fixture=root, producer=your_producer)\n14\treading.replay(out, fixture=root, expected_evidence_sha256=report[\"evidence_sha256\"])\n15\t```\n16\t\n17\t- **Producer protocol.** Your producer gets a `ProducerCall` with the\n18\t  section's bytes, its digest and the open questions on it, and answers\n19\t  `accepted`, `empty` or `refused` with facts. The loop counts the calls.\n20\t- **Stop rule per document.** `document_budget` bounds the bytes read from\n21\t  each source, beside the global `budget`; each source gets its own stop\n22\t  reason in the report's `documents`. A document whose required questions\n23\t  are answered still gets its other scheduled reads.\n24\t- **Caps as parameters.** `ReadingLimits` makes seven caps parameters: the\n25\t  roster, the largest budget, the per-file input, the response, the route\n26\t  timeout, the route output and the retained file. Each defaults to today's\n27\t  value and has a hard ceiling.\n28\t- **Replay against your root.** `replay(out, fixture=root)` re-derives the\n29\t  run with no producer call, from the settings and tables the run kept.\n30\t- Steps your profile does not declare (review, calibration, conflict,\n31\t  absence) are recorded `skipped`, never as passed. The exits of `verify`\n32\t  and `check` on your model are recorded (0, 1, 2 or 4); a completed run is\n33\t  not a verified one, and your host gates on those exits.\n34\t\n35\tNot done here: the run over your corpus with a provider budget stays with\n36\tthe literature-identity follow-up. Everything is described in\n37\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/reading_fixture/README.md`, \"Drive it from your\n38\thost\".\n39\t\n40\t## #215: admit your own assertion entity\n41\t\n42\t`assertion_admission.admit()` now takes a shape and rules:\n43\t\n44\t```python\n45\tshape = {\"format\": \"literature-assertion-shape/1\", \"assertion\": \"claim\", \"follow\": [\"quantity\"]}\n46\trules = {\"format\": \"literature-admission-rules/1\", \"requirements\": [\n47\t    {\"id\": \"positive\", \"fact_type\": \"claim_polarity\", \"role\": \"polarity\",\n48\t     \"admissible\": [\"asserts\"], \"reasons\": [{\"value\": \"negates\", \"reason\": \"negated\"}]}]}\n49\tadmission.admit(model, raw, policy, receipts, evidence, out, shape=shape, rules=rules, max_targets=512)\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t- **Identity** is your assertion entity's own handle.\n53\t- **Every fact row of an admitted assertion is kept**: every fact type the\n54\t  entity plays a role in, plus the facts of the entity types you list in\n55\t  `follow`, such as a quantity with its value and unit.\n56\t- **Optional roles are optional**: an assertion with no row of a fact type\n57\t  simply has none, and no value means \"absent\".\n58\t- **Polarity and attribution rules are data**, with a distinct status: a\n59\t  reviewed assertion your rules refuse is `policy-refused`, not `fail`.\n60\t- **`max_targets`** is a parameter.\n61\t- Include roots are admitted with their includes.\n62\t\n63\tNot done here, by decision: 1,024 targets per call is `gnd judgments\n64\tcheck`'s own cap, so a larger set is admitted in several calls. An entity\n65\tthat objectifies a fact type is refused, so an assertion needs its own\n66\thandle. Following an entity type you do not list is not done. If your model\n67\tdoes not fit these, say so here. The shape, the rules and the record are\n68\tdescribed in `src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md`, \"Admitting your own\n69\tassertion entity\"."}
